Z||000000||Thor||08-29-2000||11:57 PM||||I'v been brousing these pages and posted messages for weeks now.  All because [A].My parking light fuse blew ALMOST every time I switched them on or while I was Driving. B.When I turned on the headlights they would come on and rise but when I shut them off the lights would stay on and not go down. If I turned the parking light switch on again,the lights would turn off but not go down. When I turned the parking switch off again,the headlights would go down. [If I blew the fuse the lights would go off but they would not go down unless I replaced the fuse with the light switch off]. Look for any posts hosted by Thor over the last 30 days if you want to investigate my questions. <BR>What I did to solve [A]Seporated the connection for the harness that led to the rear of the car[On my 86GT it was located just rearward and above the battery.] The fuse did not blow. As it turned out in my case it was a frayed license plate bulb socket wire that sometimes came in contact with the frame. Repaired the wire and WALLA! I was legal to drive at night again.<BR>What I did to solve [B]. Replaced the isolation relay located on the frame right next to the driver side headlight...ALL IS WELL! I hope this information helps some of you who are having the same or similar problems. THANK YOU ALL FOR HELPING ME GET THROUGH THESE VEXING PROBLEMS.<BR> ||||reg||6
